+## Projection GEMM search
+
+The ignored `gemm_cuda::bench::measure_cua_s1_gemms` test compares Candle's
+default bias-free BF16 linear projection with up to 32 cuBLASLt heuristics,
+using F32 compute and the existing 64 MiB scratch workspace. It needs CUDA but
+no checkpoint. It covers M=200, 1400 and 1860 for all remaining projection
+shapes; projections with the same dimensions share a row (15 rows total).
+The CUTLASS SwiGLU gate/up projection is excluded.
+
+```sh
+VS1_CUA_S1_GEMM_OUTPUT=artifacts/cua-s1/gemm-search.json \
+  direnv exec . cargo test --release -p vs1 --features cuda --lib \
+  gemm_cuda::bench::measure_cua_s1_gemms -- --ignored --exact --nocapture --test-threads=1
+```
+
+Each candidate and the baseline get two warmup calls followed by 21 separately
+synchronized CUDA-event samples; the reported time is their median in ms.
+Timing uses the normal output-allocation path and excludes heuristic queries,
+random input generation and bit comparisons. Inputs are seeded random BF16
+activations and weights at the real matrix sizes. Exactness compares raw BF16
+output bits with Candle on those inputs; it does not gate the fastest candidate.
+
+Each row prints as JSON and is saved with GPU, library and measurement metadata
+to `VS1_CUA_S1_GEMM_OUTPUT` (required, relative to the workspace root unless
+absolute). The file is updated after each completed row. Rows include the actual
+heuristic count, all candidate configurations, timings, speedups and exactness,
+plus the best candidate. Failed candidates retain their errors and null values
+for unavailable measurements; no usable candidate leaves `best_candidate` null.
+This experiment does not change production dispatch.
+
