+# G3c: runtime projection GEMM tuning
+
+CUDA/BF16 decoder projections share a mutex-protected cache per text model.
+The key contains N, K, M, weight strides, dtype and Candle's BF16 reduction
+setting. The cache is tied to its CUDA device. Biases, noncontiguous tensors,
+unaligned offsets and other dtypes use Candle directly. CUTLASS SwiGLU and
+the encoder's Retile behavior are unchanged.
+
+The first call measures Candle and up to eight cuBLASLt heuristic candidates
+on the actual input and weights. Each measurement has one warmup and three
+single-GEMM CUDA-event samples; selection uses the median. Candle is measured
+again afterward, taking the faster baseline to limit clock warmup bias.
+A candidate must take at most 97% of that baseline time. Unsupported candidates
+are skipped. Both default and non-default choices are cached across layers;
+cache hits perform no timing or heuristic query.
+
+Tuning costs at most 40 trial GEMMs per key, plus descriptor/event setup and
+synchronization, using one 64 MiB scratch buffer per model. The actual elapsed
+cost cannot be measured in the CPU-only development environment.
+`vs1::cua_s1::read_gemm_tuning_stats()` exposes process totals for `keys_tuned`,
+`non_default_keys` and wall-clock `tuning_time` (including initial scratch
+allocation and GPU waits). The CUDA CLI prints these totals after inference.
+Set `VS1_CUA_S1_GEMM_AUTOTUNE=0` before loading the model to always use Candle.
+Autotuning is enabled by default.
+
+The ignored test uses real down, QKV/query and small a/b projection dimensions
+at M = 1152 and 1860, with seeded normal inputs and scaled normal weights. It
+checks the chosen output against Candle with `atol = rtol = 2^-6`, prints each
+choice, measured speedup and tuning time, and checks cache reuse across weights
+and host threads plus the disabled path:
+
+```sh
+direnv exec . cargo test -p vs1 --features cuda tunes_cua_s1_projections_within_bf16_tolerance -- --ignored --nocapture --test-threads=1
+```
+
+This test is compiled only here. The dispatcher still needs to run it and
+measure model parity and warm end-to-end latency with autotuning on and off.
